      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "As-cast HfMoTaTiZr has a single-phase BCC microstructure.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "As-cast HfMoTaTiZr has a room-temperature yield strength of approximately 1600 MPa.",
      "field": "baseline",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "As-cast HfMoTaTiZr has a yield strength of approximately 855 MPa at 1000 °C.",
      "field": "baseline",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Replacing approximately 25 wt.% of Hf with V results in the composition (Hf0.75V0.25)MoTaTiZr.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Conventional melting and casting with controlled cooling can produce a homogeneous single-phase solid solution of the modified alloy.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Vanadium has a significantly lower density than hafnium.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Partial substitution of Hf by V reduces average atomic mass and consequently reduces alloy density.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The atomic radii of V and Hf are sufficiently similar, and the resulting atomic-size mismatch is acceptable for retaining the BCC matrix.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC9586648::web::012::strategy_to_optimize_refractory_alloy_st"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The modified alloy will retain atomic-scale lattice distortion.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC9586648::web::012::strategy_to_optimize_refractory_alloy_st"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Retained lattice distortion and favorable dislocation mobility will preserve solid-solution strengthening and both room- and high-temperature strength.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC9586648::web::012::strategy_to_optimize_refractory_alloy_st"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The modified alloy will retain a homogeneous single-phase BCC structure.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The modified alloy will have a density 10–15% below that of as-cast HfMoTaTiZr.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The modified alloy's room-temperature yield strength will remain within ±10% of 1600 MPa.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The modified alloy's yield strength at 1000 °C will remain within ±10% of 855 MPa.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Ductility will remain comparable to the baseline if the single-phase BCC structure is maintained.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Mechanical performance will be evaluated in quasi-static tension at room temperature and 1000 °C at approximately 10^-3 s^-1.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "These tensile conditions represent realistic service conditions.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
